A||N||4||2xsess||85GT 4spd to 5spd swap opinions needed||||5||
Z||000000||2xsess||11-04-2000||01:20 PM||||I know where I can get a getrag out of an 86.5 GT, I was thinking of swapping the 5spd into my 85GT. I know the syncros in the getrag are the weak link. I 'm not really worried about fuel economy since I really only drive my Fiero around town. And I really have no complaints about the 4spd but the price on the getrag is too good to pass up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And also I'm going to have to put a new slave on my 4spd anyways and I need to drop the cradle to fix the exhaust manifold.<P>What is everyones opinion on this swap.<P>TIA <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 11-04-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||11-04-2000||01:41 PM||||Plan to get the shifter and cables out of the 1986.5 GT also, if you want to use the Getrag.  Remember the backup light switch is in the console for the 4-speed; it's in the transaxle for the Getrag, so you'll have a little rewiring to do.<P>The Muncie 4-speed is supposed to be the most bulletproof, so if it works well now, you might just want to stick with it.  On the other hand, if it's really such a good deal, it'd be nice to have an extra transaxle around just in case!  You might even resell it at a profit  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !    ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MikeE||11-04-2000||04:23 PM||||I've commented on this before so it may be academic and it probably doesn't really matter anyway.<P>According to a fellow on the performance34dohc list, he called Getrag in Detroit to ask about the Muncie 282 5sp trans used in 85 & up V6 Fieros.  They had never heard of the trans and apparently never made or designed the 5 speed trans used in V6 Fieros.  They did design the Getrag 284 found in GM cars with the 3.4 DOHC V6 but no longer make perts or cases which is causing those guys some problems and has resulted in their swaping in the Muncie 282 from Fieros and other GM cars.<P>Does anyone now how and why everyone started calling the trans a Getrag?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||11-04-2000||08:55 PM||||i thought i'd heard once that getrag designed it but muncie made it?<P>how do you get to this 3.4 dohc list?||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||11-04-2000||10:27 PM||||Phil has it right about tranny name and origin.||||reg||1
